WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:05.211
Hello, everyone! I'm Ms. Emma. Welcome to Online Grammar, level C one.

2
00:00:05.511 --> 00:00:08.990
Hi! I'm Visal. Let's learn together!

3
00:00:09.290 --> 00:00:15.066
Unit sixteen: Advanced Conditional Inversion. Today you will write formal conditionals without 'if'.

4
00:00:15.366 --> 00:00:18.099
Here is our lesson map. Let's start!

5
00:00:19.033 --> 00:00:22.394
Part one: words. You will learn eight new words.

6
00:00:23.250 --> 00:00:23.984
Should you.

7
00:00:24.983 --> 00:00:27.772
Should you means a formal replacement for if you should.

8
00:00:28.383 --> 00:00:30.418
Should you need help, call me.

9
00:00:31.017 --> 00:00:33.715
Your turn. Say: Should you.

10
00:00:36.567 --> 00:00:37.637
Should you.

11
00:00:38.383 --> 00:00:39.512
Were you to.

12
00:00:40.517 --> 00:00:43.294
Were you to means a formal replacement for if you were to.

13
00:00:43.883 --> 00:00:45.546
Were you to leave, I would miss you.

14
00:00:46.150 --> 00:00:48.628
Your turn. Say: Were you to.

15
00:00:51.467 --> 00:00:52.491
Were you to.

16
00:00:53.250 --> 00:00:54.634
Had it not been.

17
00:00:55.650 --> 00:00:59.252
Had it not been means a formal replacement for if it had not been.

18
00:00:59.850 --> 00:01:02.024
Had it not been for you, I would have failed.

19
00:01:02.617 --> 00:01:05.362
Your turn. Say: Had it not been.

20
00:01:08.200 --> 00:01:09.410
Had it not been.

21
00:01:10.150 --> 00:01:11.360
Formal inversion.

22
00:01:12.350 --> 00:01:15.754
Formal inversion means reversing words in a formal text.

23
00:01:16.350 --> 00:01:17.920
A formal inversion.

24
00:01:18.517 --> 00:01:21.401
Your turn. Say: Formal inversion.

25
00:01:24.267 --> 00:01:25.546
Formal inversion.

26
00:01:26.283 --> 00:01:27.702
Conditional without if.

27
00:01:28.717 --> 00:01:31.750
Conditional without if means a conditional that omits if.

28
00:01:32.350 --> 00:01:33.897
A conditional without if.

29
00:01:34.483 --> 00:01:37.681
Your turn. Say: Conditional without if.

30
00:01:40.533 --> 00:01:41.941
Conditional without if.

31
00:01:42.683 --> 00:01:44.114
Subjunctive inversion.

32
00:01:45.117 --> 00:01:47.836
Subjunctive inversion means an inversion with were.

33
00:01:48.450 --> 00:01:49.985
Subjunctive inversion.

34
00:01:50.583 --> 00:01:53.421
Your turn. Say: Subjunctive inversion.

35
00:01:56.267 --> 00:01:58.162
Subjunctive inversion.

36
00:01:58.917 --> 00:02:00.127
Elevated tone.

37
00:02:01.117 --> 00:02:03.941
Elevated tone means a serious, high style.

38
00:02:04.550 --> 00:02:06.039
An elevated tone.

39
00:02:06.650 --> 00:02:09.639
Your turn. Say: Elevated tone.

40
00:02:12.500 --> 00:02:13.826
Elevated tone.

41
00:02:14.583 --> 00:02:15.979
Literary conditional.

42
00:02:16.983 --> 00:02:20.190
Literary conditional means an elegant conditional in writing.

43
00:02:20.783 --> 00:02:22.458
A literary conditional.

44
00:02:23.050 --> 00:02:26.062
Your turn. Say: Literary conditional.

45
00:02:28.900 --> 00:02:30.540
Literary conditional.

46
00:02:31.333 --> 00:02:34.914
Part two: dialogue. Let's listen to a conversation.

47
00:02:35.750 --> 00:02:40.211
Visal, how does a formal notice say If you should need help, please call?

48
00:02:41.317 --> 00:02:53.422
Should you need help, please call. We drop if and put should before the subject. It sounds polite and professional, so it is common in emails and instructions.

49
00:02:54.517 --> 00:02:56.470
And for imaginary situations?

50
00:02:57.583 --> 00:03:07.019
Were you to accept the offer, you would earn more. That means If you were to accept. Were it not for the rain... means If it were not for the rain.

51
00:03:08.117 --> 00:03:09.896
Is the past form different?

52
00:03:10.983 --> 00:03:23.530
Yes. Had it not been for your help, I would have failed uses had for the past. Remember the three: should for possible, were for unreal present, had for unreal past.

53
00:03:24.667 --> 00:03:26.353
Part three: grammar.

54
00:03:27.217 --> 00:03:32.421
Grammar focus: Conditional inversion: Should and Were and Had plus subject, main clause.

55
00:03:32.721 --> 00:03:33.977
Look at the pattern.

56
00:03:34.683 --> 00:03:36.602
Should you need help, please call me.

57
00:03:37.517 --> 00:03:39.795
Were you to accept, you would earn more.

58
00:03:40.683 --> 00:03:42.927
Had it not been for you, I would have failed.

59
00:03:43.867 --> 00:03:52.422
Should = possible. Were you to = unreal present or future. Had it not been = unreal past. Never use if after inversion.

60
00:03:53.183 --> 00:03:56.915
Be careful! Don't say: Should you to need help, call.

61
00:03:58.867 --> 00:04:00.878
Say: Should you need help, call.

62
00:04:01.178 --> 00:04:02.701
No to after should.

63
00:04:03.500 --> 00:04:06.292
Part four: reading. Read and listen.

64
00:04:07.100 --> 00:04:08.264
Dear Customer.

65
00:04:08.564 --> 00:04:11.724
Should you require assistance, please contact our office.

66
00:04:12.733 --> 00:04:15.058
Were you to cancel now, a fee would apply.

67
00:04:16.067 --> 00:04:18.798
Had we known about the problem, we would have acted sooner.

68
00:04:19.800 --> 00:04:22.287
Should the delay continue, we will inform you.

69
00:04:23.300 --> 00:04:26.646
Formal inversion makes official letters sound polite and clear.

70
00:04:27.733 --> 00:04:31.619
Part five: quiz. Five questions. Are you ready?

71
00:04:32.483 --> 00:04:34.239
blank you need help, call me.

72
00:04:34.539 --> 00:04:37.461
A, Should. B, Would. C, Did.

73
00:04:41.000 --> 00:04:42.779
The answer is A: Should.

74
00:04:43.917 --> 00:04:45.730
blank you to leave, I would miss you.

75
00:04:46.030 --> 00:04:49.266
A, Was. B, Were. C, Be.

76
00:04:52.800 --> 00:04:54.335
The answer is B: Were.

77
00:04:55.483 --> 00:04:57.703
blank it not been for you, I would have failed.

78
00:04:58.003 --> 00:05:00.925
A, Had. B, Have. C, If.

79
00:05:04.467 --> 00:05:05.932
The answer is A: Had.

80
00:05:07.083 --> 00:05:09.675
Conditional inversion removes the word blank.

81
00:05:09.975 --> 00:05:12.792
A, if. B, not. C, that.

82
00:05:16.333 --> 00:05:18.019
The answer is A: if.

83
00:05:19.183 --> 00:05:22.402
According to the reading, what would apply if you cancelled?

84
00:05:22.702 --> 00:05:26.576
A, a fee. B, a prize. C, a discount.

85
00:05:30.133 --> 00:05:31.936
The answer is A: a fee.

86
00:05:33.133 --> 00:05:36.598
Part six: speaking. It's your turn to talk.

87
00:05:37.450 --> 00:05:41.226
Write a formal conditional sentence using inversion instead of 'if'.

88
00:05:50.017 --> 00:05:51.424
Now listen to Visal.

89
00:05:51.724 --> 00:06:01.775
Should you wish to join the club, please complete the form. Were the club to grow, we would need a bigger room. I use inversion to sound polite and formal.

90
00:06:02.075 --> 00:06:03.865
Excellent answer, Visal!

91
00:06:04.750 --> 00:06:12.162
Great work! Now you can use eight new words and conditional inversion: should and were and had plus subject, main clause.

92
00:06:12.462 --> 00:06:17.460
Today's value is practical wisdom. Judge ideas by how well they work in real life.

93
00:06:17.760 --> 00:06:20.610
See you in Unit seventeen. Goodbye!

94
00:06:20.910 --> 00:06:23.817
Thank you, Ms. Emma! Bye, everyone!

